%9Setting:%9

    disk_warn (size; default: 20M)

%9Description:%9

    erssi says in the Notices window when less than disk_warn is left for
    its home: the free space of the home's file system, or what your disk
    quota there leaves (the soft limit if one is set), the smaller one. It
    looks a few seconds after the start and every 10 minutes, and says it
    again every 6 hours while it stays low. A full disk or quota stops
    logs, the E2E keyring (a message that needs a new key is not sent)
    and backups. 0 turns the warning off.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET disk_warn 20M
    /SET disk_warn 100M
    /SET disk_warn 0

%9See also:%9 BACKUP, BACKUP_AUTO
